# Engineering POC

This isolated POC experiments with an agentic software-engineering loop around
a small task-board application. Codex owns code inspection, edits, reasoning,
and failure interpretation. The companion MCP server owns only fixed
application lifecycle and verification operations.

## Dev Container

Open `engineering-poc` in VS Code and choose **Dev Containers: Reopen in
Container**. The container uses Python 3.12, Node 22, Docker, and Playwright.
Project dependencies are installed by the dev-container `postCreateCommand`,
not on the host.

## Local App Checks

From inside the dev container:

```bash
docker compose build
docker compose up -d backend frontend
docker compose run --rm backend-tests
docker compose run --rm ui-tests
```

The application is available at `http://localhost:4173`.

## MCP Image

Build and run the standalone stdio MCP server independently:

```bash
docker compose build mcp
docker compose run --rm mcp
```

The MCP container is intentionally not connected to the existing Docker MCP
profile. It uses the local Docker socket only so its four fixed tools can
control this Compose project during the POC.

